{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966788,"nonce":"iWpKlK3EnCiK3eq1un2UUsRlirI=","title":"Polygon clip / 3D-group aux_data must follow batch routing into dynamic_batch, and","message":"When the walker emits a primitive inside a motion-bound subtree (`push_motion_subtree` depth \u003e 0), the primitive routes into `GpuPaintContext::dynamic_batch`. Variable-length data referenced by that primitive — polygon-clip vertices (`clip_radius.w` offset), 3D-group shape descriptors (`border[2]` offset), `triangle_mesh` packed vertices — has to live in the SAME batch so the offsets resolve at draw time.\n\n**Why:** Pre-fix, `GpuPaintContext::push_clip` for polygon shapes wrote vertices to `self.batch.aux_data` (the static batch) regardless of `motion_subtree_depth`. The primitive itself routed correctly into `dynamic_batch.primitives`, but its `aux_offset` indexed `static_batch.aux_data` — which gets uploaded once into the GPU storage buffer for the static-cache pass, then OVERWRITTEN by the static-cache pass's content. The overlay dispatch then reads stale / wrong vertex data and the polygon-clip discard misses. Symptom in `cn_demo`: spinner gray ring renders but rotating arc doesn't (the polygon mask collapses to \"no clip\" / \"all-discard\"). Spinner_test was accidentally working because the static batch happened to have only the spinner's polygon vertices and no other aux_data.\n\n**How to apply:**\n1. In `paint::push_clip`, write polygon vertices via `active_batch_mut().aux_data.push(...)` so the same routing applies — same for any future `push_*` that lays down aux_data.\n2. `GpuRenderer::composite_frame` takes an `overlay_aux_data: \u0026[[f32; 4]]` slice and re-uploads it via `update_aux_data_buffer` before dispatching overlay primitives. The static-cache pass's aux_data has already been baked into the cached texture, so overwriting is safe.\n3. Both call sites in `blinc_app::context` (`use_fast` branch and the post-walker slow path) clone `cached_dynamic_batch.aux_data` and pass it in. Canvas closures still drop their aux_data on the floor (`collect_canvas_overlay` ignores `new_batch.aux_data`); canvas closures don't currently emit polygon clips or 3D groups, so this is latent but not yet a visible bug. Phase 3 of the Compositor v2 plan will replace this whole path with per-region dispatch.\n\nSee [[gotcha-fast-path-visible-anim-latch]] and [[gotcha-canvas-fast-path-freeze]] for adjacent compositor-fast-path gotchas.","files":null}]}